{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The fare breakdown charges SGD 2.00 for the 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry', but this trip's own GPS trace never goes near that gantry. The derived gantry-proximity analysis puts the closest fix to the gantry's coordinates at 4,851.46 m away, and records that no gap in the trace brackets a closest approach to it. POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to a trace by treating any fix within 250 m as a crossing; at roughly nineteen times that radius, not a single one of the 107 fixes is a crossing. A charge line for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), refunded in full as a standalone correction.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03208", "EV-FARE-03208"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not need to win a route-deviation finding to recover this line: POL-RD-09(4) makes the billing-integrity correction available whether or not a deviation exists. The record in fact shows the deviation is NOT established, and the rider does not pretend otherwise - the derived figures give an excess of 0.65 km and 5.04%, and POL-RD-01 requires an excess greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20% before a deviation exists. Both tests fail, so no POL-RD-02 distance refund arises. The rider's case is confined to the phantom gantry line, and it succeeds on its own footing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03208", "EV-TRIP-03208"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The platform's own routing confirms the gantry sits on no route it ever planned for this trip. The trip record's optimal route carries zero ERP (optimal_route_erp_sgd = 0.0), and the fare breakdown's money block books SGD 0.00 of ERP as on-optimal-route and the entire SGD 2.00 as off-optimal-route, with the gantry line itself flagged on_optimal_route = false. A gantry that is neither on the planned route nor anywhere near the driven trace has no basis to be billed to this rider at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-03208", "EV-FARE-03208"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.off_optimal_route_total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The counterparty's entire answer is 'The ERP is charged by the system.' That assertion points to no artifact and no measurement, and under POL-RD-08 an assertion from either side that cites no evidence ID carries no weight and is discarded. It cannot convert a trace whose nearest approach to the gantry is 4.85 km into a crossing, and it supplies no artifact that could corroborate the charge line.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03208"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not a case where a fare-breakdown line has baffled the record so that POL-RD-10(8) must send it to a human. POL-RD-09(4) expressly provides that POL-RD-10(8) is NOT triggered where the only unmatched line is one refunded under that limb, and the policy's own commentary records the reason: a phantom line is both refundable and knowable, so the tribunal rules on it. The single unmatched line here is exactly that line, so the ruling should issue and the money should move.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03208", "EV-GPS-03208"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.lines[0].trace_proximity.nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The proximity measurement rests on a clean instrument. The GPS artifact is COMPLETE at a weight multiplier of 1.0: 107 fixes at a 10 s sample interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 s. POL-RD-07's impairment limbs (a) to (c) are therefore not engaged, no straight-line-across-gap discount applies, and the 4,851.46 m nearest-approach figure can be taken at full weight under POL-GEN-02.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03208"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory is on file for this trip that could excuse any running outside the planned corridor. EV-ADVIS-03208-01 is MISSING - admissibility status MISSING, weight multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, with the note that no advisory covers the Blk 412 Pasir Ris Dr 6 corridor in this window. The rider cites that absence precisely because it is citable: with no advisory covering the trip window, the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run and any external-traffic explanation carries no weight under POL-RD-08 (POL-RD-13). Nothing in the bundle justifies a gantry charge the trace does not support. This claim relies on an artifact of weight 0.0 and does not ask it to carry any fact about the trip - only its own absence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-03208-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On quantum, the whole of the amount the rider contested comes back. The disputed line is SGD 2.00 and the correction under POL-RD-09(4) refunds it in full as a standalone item, comfortably above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and unaffected by the POL-RD-02 recomputation because no deviation is established. The rider's charge should not stand and the present state of the ledger should not be preserved under POL-GEN-03; the rider asks for the SGD 2.00 to be returned and a billing-integrity finding to be recorded in the ruling's referrals list - a referral, not an escalation, so the refund issues rather than being held.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03208", "EV-GPS-03208"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the SGD 2.00 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' ERP line on TRP-03208 was charged for a gantry the GPS trace (EV-GPS-03208) never crosses — the closest of the 107 fixes lies 4,851.46 m from the gantry coordinates against the 250 m match radius — and is refunded in full as a standalone correction."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and Driver — this decision concerns the SGD 2.00 ERP line disputed on trip TRP-03208. It divides into two questions, and they come out differently.\n\n1) Was there a route deviation? No. Measured on the governing trace figure, gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 13.55 km (EV-GPS-03208), against the booked optimal of 12.9 km (EV-TRIP-03208), the excess is 0.65 km, or 5.04%. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20% of the optimal; both tests fail, so no deviation exists and no POL-RD-02 distance-or-time refund is available. The trace is COMPLETE and unimpaired — 107 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0 s — so POL-RD-07 imposes no gap discount and no corroboration requirement, and no POL-RD-10(3) trigger fires. The Driver's claims that no deviation is established, that the trace figure governs over trip_record.actual_distance_km, and that no repeat-deviation pattern applies (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 0 against completed_trips_90d = 216, so POL-RD-06 gives no uplift and no conduct referral) are accepted.\n\n2) Does the SGD 2.00 ERP line survive? No. POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to the trace by treating any fix within 250 m of the gantry's coordinates as a crossing. The gantry coordinates come from the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-03208); the closest of the trace's 107 fixes lies 4,851.46 m from them, and no gap in the trace brackets a closest approach. The platform's own routing agrees: trip_record.optimal_route_erp_sgd = 0.0; the fare breakdown books SGD 0.00 of ERP as on-optimal-route and the entire SGD 2.00 as off-optimal-route; and the gantry line itself is flagged on_optimal_route = false. A charge line for a gantry the trace never passes (or is never within 250 m of) is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), refunded in full as a standalone correction, and that correction is available whether or not a deviation exists.\n\nThe Driver's answer — 'The ERP is charged by the system.' — points to no artifact and no measurement; under POL-RD-08 an assertion that cites no evidence ID carries no weight, and it cannot turn a nearest approach of 4.85 km into a crossing. The Driver's further contention that the gantry match 'decides no match' because the 250 m radius is a prose-only field is rejected: POL-RD-09 states that radius in terms and the geometry is already computed, so the match is run and it fails. For the same reasons the Driver's request for NO_ACTION is rejected — the present state should not be preserved for a line the trace does not support.\n\nNo escalation. POL-RD-10(8) is not engaged: POL-RD-09(4) states expressly that it is not triggered where the only unmatched fare line is one refunded under that limb, and the single unmatched line here is exactly that. No POL-RD-10(5) trigger fires: no party invoked a closure or other exculpatory clause against the absent traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-03208-01, status MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) — the advisory simply does not exist for this window, and the rider cites its absence only to note it, which under POL-RD-13 is not an escalation. POL-RD-09(1) is respected: off-route ERP is not added on top of any POL-RD-02 figure, because no POL-RD-02 refund exists; the SGD 2.00 moves as a standalone pass-through correction instead.\n\nWhat moves. The contested amount is SGD 2.00 (the ERP line) and the refund is SGD 2.00, being the whole of it, so the outcome is FULL_REFUND. The monetary effect (SGD 2.00) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05) and executes automatically on issue. Every artifact this ruling rests on carries weight 1.0 (EV-GPS-03208, EV-FARE-03208), so no POL-GEN-02 discount applies. A billing-integrity referral under POL-RD-09(4) is recorded below; it rides with the refund and does not hold it."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4): record a billing-integrity finding — the SGD 2.00 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' ERP line was charged although the GPS trace never passes within 250 m of the gantry (nearest fix 4,851.46 m; fare breakdown books the line as on_optimal_route = false)."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider: the SGD 2.00 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' ERP charge is refunded in full. Your GPS trace (EV-GPS-03208) is complete and clean — 107 fixes at 10-second intervals, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s — so it is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07. Its closest fix to the gantry's coordinates (lat 1.311147, lng 103.872638) is 4,851.46 m away. POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to the trace only where a fix comes within 250 m; nothing comes within nineteen times that radius. The fare breakdown itself (EV-FARE-03208) books the line as on_optimal_route = false and records SGD 0.00 of on-optimal-route ERP against SGD 2.00 off-optimal-route. A charge for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), refunded in full as a standalone correction, and it is available whether or not a deviation exists. The whole contested amount is returned: FULL_REFUND of SGD 2.00, with a billing-integrity finding referred under POL-RD-09(4).\n\nTo the driver: your distance is not in question. The trace shows 13.55 km against a booked optimal of 12.9 km — an excess of 0.65 km, or 5.04%, below both the 0.8 km and the 20% tests in POL-RD-01 — so no deviation is established and no POL-RD-02 distance-or-time refund runs. Both sides agree on that. But the ERP line is a separate matter. Your statement that 'The ERP is charged by the system' cites no evidence ID and carries no weight under POL-RD-08 — the system's charge is the very thing tested — and the billing-integrity limb is not left undecided: the gantry's own coordinates and the trace decide it. The money block's note that the 250 m match radius is not a structured field means the derivation published no match; it does not stop the clause being applied by hand, and the 4,851.46 m figure is nowhere near the limit. Your argument that the rider 'has not put a match determination in evidence' is rejected: the rider cites the trace and the gantry coordinates, and the policy's own radius rule decides the comparison.\n\nOn the remaining points: no traffic advisory covers this trip (EV-ADVIS-03208-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0), so POL-RD-03 is unavailable and no closure-adjusted optimal exists (POL-RD-13). No repeat-deviation pattern is engaged (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 0 against 216 completed trips), so no POL-RD-06 uplift, balance-shift or conduct referral follows; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags may not be substituted for the trailing-90-day field. POL-RD-10 escalation does not fire: the trace is unimpaired, the trip identifiers (TRP-03208) match across trip record, trace and fare breakdown, and the only unmatched charge line is the one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly excludes.\n\nThis ruling rests on EV-GPS-03208 and EV-FARE-03208, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, which carry the deciding fact independently; confidence 0.95. The SGD 2.00 refund is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold and executes on issue, subject to appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4): billing-integrity finding - the SGD 2.00 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' ERP line on trip TRP-03208 is unmatched to the trip's own GPS trace (closest of 107 fixes is 4,851.46 m from the gantry, far outside the 250 m crossing radius, and no gap brackets a closest approach); the line is refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Decision on trip TRP-03208 (RIDER RDR-10208 v DRIVER DRV-10208). Two questions were on the table: whether the driver deviated from the planned route, and whether the SGD 2.00 ERP line billed to the rider was properly chargeable. They come out differently, and both parties should read the whole of this.\\n\\nThe deviation defence succeeds. POL-RD-01 measures the trace between the recorded pickup and dropoff: gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 13.55 km against a booked optimal of 12.9 km, an excess of 0.65 km, or 5.04% - below both the 0.8 km absolute and the 20% proportional tests, which must pass together. No deviation is established, so POL-RD-02 never runs and no distance-or-time refund is due on that ground. The trace is also clean for policy purposes: 107 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s, so POL-RD-07 limbs (a)-(c) do not fire and there is no POL-RD-10(3) escalation. The driver's POL-RD-06 pattern check is likewise not engaged: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 216 completed trips in 90 days, and the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags may not be substituted (POL-GEN-01; the referee flagged that field as context-only).\\n\\nThe ERP line, however, does not stand. The fare breakdown books the whole SGD 2.00 as off-optimal-route ERP, charges it for the 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' at lat 1.311147, lng 103.872638, and the trip record's optimal route carries zero ERP (optimal_route_erp_sgd = 0.0). POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to a trace by treating any fix within 250 m as a crossing. The platform's own proximity analysis puts the closest of the trace's 107 fixes at 4,851.46 m from that gantry - about nineteen times the radius, with no gap bracketing a closest approach. The vehicle never crossed the gantry, so the charge is a phantom line: a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists.\\n\\nThe driver's answer, 'The ERP is charged by the system', cites no evidence ID and is discarded under POL-RD-08; it cannot convert a 4.85 km nearest approach into a crossing. The driver's argument that POL-RD-09(4) is 'not a computed finding' is rejected: the 250 m match is a field comparison the record supplies (gantry coordinates on the fare breakdown against the trace), and the match is decidable here, not undecidable. No traffic advisory covers this trip (EV-ADVIS-03208-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 is unavailable and no closure-adjusted optimal exists - both parties' claims on that point are accepted, and under POL-RD-13 no party asserted an external traffic cause against the missing advisory, so no POL-RD-10(5) escalation arises. POL-RD-10(8) is not triggered because the only unmatched line is the one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which that limb expressly excludes.\\n\\nMoney and confidence. The contested amount is SGD 2.00 within a charged_total of SGD 21.76; the correction returns the contested ERP line, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND - POL-RD-09 licenses PARTIAL_REFUND and NO_ACTION only, and this pass-through correction is a part of the fare rather than a refund of the trip. The deciding fact (the trace never passes the gantry) is carried by EV-GPS-03208 and EV-FARE-03208, both at weight_multiplier 1.0 and independent of each other, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and confidence is set at 0.90. No driver compensation arises (POL-RD-04 does not apply). The monetary effect of SGD 2.00 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the refund is executed automatically on issue subject to appeal under POL-GEN-04. Both parties may appeal once within 30 days."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity finding: the SGD 2.00 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' ERP line on TRP-03208 has no trace fix within the 250 m match radius (nearest fix 4,851.46 m) and has been refunded in full as a standalone correction; record for billing-integrity review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider, your dispute succeeds on the ERP line; Driver, the rest of the fare stands. The contested SGD 2.00 is the 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' ERP line on fare breakdown EV-FARE-03208. POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to the trip's GPS trace by treating any fix within 250 m of the gantry's coordinates as a crossing. That gantry carries coordinates (lat 1.311147, lng 103.872638), and across all 107 fixes of trace EV-GPS-03208 the closest approach is 4,851.46 m, roughly nineteen times the radius. No fix is a crossing, so the line is a phantom charge and POL-RD-09(4) refunds it in full as a standalone billing-integrity correction, available whether or not a deviation exists. The platform's own money block agrees: on-optimal-route ERP is SGD 0.00 and the whole SGD 2.00 is booked off-route, with optimal_route_erp_sgd at 0.0. On the route-deviation question both advocates agree and so do I: the governing trace distance is 13.55 km against a booked optimal of 12.9 km, an excess of 0.65 km (5.04%), below both the 0.8 km and the 20% thresholds in POL-RD-01, whose test must use the trace figure rather than the rounded trip-record copy. No deviation is established, so no POL-RD-02 recomputation runs and no distance or time refund arises. That does not touch the ERP line, and because no POL-RD-02 refund exists, POL-RD-09(1)'s anti-double-count rule has nothing to subtract: the SGD 2.00 is a standalone correction, not an add-on. The Driver's argument that the money block 'decides no match' and that the rider put no match determination in evidence is rejected: the match test is the one POL-RD-09 states (250 m), and the record supplies both the gantry's coordinates and the nearest-fix distance, so the comparison runs and returns no crossing. The Driver's on-file statement, 'The ERP is charged by the system,' cites no artifact and carries no weight under POL-RD-08; it cannot turn a 4,851 m nearest approach into a crossing. The trace is clean: 107 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 s, so the POL-RD-07(a)-(c) impairment limbs are not engaged and no escalation discount applies. No traffic advisory covers this trip (EV-ADVIS-03208-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0), so POL-RD-03 is unavailable; but no party asserted an external traffic cause, so POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-10(5) are not engaged. Because the only unmatched charge line is the one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), POL-RD-10(8) is not triggered and the case does not escalate. No repeat-deviation pattern is engaged: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 216 completed trips in 90 days, below both POL-RD-06 limbs, so there is no remedy uplift and no conduct referral; POL-GEN-01 prevents substituting the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter. Amount: contested SGD 2.00, refunded SGD 2.00 - the whole contested amount, so this is a full refund. The refund is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis. The monetary effect (SGD 2.00) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically. Confidence is 0.95: the deciding facts rest on EV-GPS-03208 and EV-FARE-03208, both at weight 1.0. One referral issues under POL-RD-09(4) recording the billing-integrity finding."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
